body:
The ordering assertion can pass even if the tool-call event is missing, because `findIndex` returns `-1` and `-1` is still less than any valid tool-result index. Add an explicit assertion that a tool-call event exists (e.g., expect(toolCallIdx).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(0) / expect(events.some(...)).toBe(true)) before comparing indices.
```suggestion
    const toolResultIdx = events.findIndex(e => e.type === 'tool-result');
    expect(toolCallIdx).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(0);
    expect(toolResultIdx).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(0);
```
